jobs.content:
&lt;h2 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;About Epic&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Epic Kids is the leading digital reading platform built for kids 12 and under, trusted by millions of children, educators, and families around the world. Our mission is to inspire a lifelong love of reading by providing unlimited access to thousands of high-quality books, videos, and educational content through a safe and engaging experience. We combine technology, storytelling, and learning innovation to help every child become a confident reader.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Epic, you&#39;ll join a collaborative and fast-paced global team passionate about building meaningful products that make a real impact on children&#39;s education and literacy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring a hands-on, detail-driven Conference and Educator Events Coordinator to manage our growing conference calendar from contract to close-out. This is a temporary W2 position for 6 months, with the option to extend, requiring 35 to 40 hours per week. Reporting to the Educator Engagement Lead, the ideal candidate will have 3 to 5 years of event operations experience, a proven ability to manage multiple events simultaneously, and a strong attention to detail to ensure nothing is late, lost, or missing. The target start date is mid-November 2026.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You Will Own&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conference planning and logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Manage end-to-end conference operations across an annual calendar of 10 to 12 events (FETC, TCEA, ISTE, ASU+GSV, NCTE, BETT and others), with several shows in planning at once. Own booth logistics, shipping, vendor coordination, swag and giveaway procurement, and travel for staff and Epic Educator Fellows. Track sponsorship deliverables and deadlines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Booth design and educator experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Help shape the next version of the Epic booth: research display and signage options, vendors and costs, and coordinate with our creative team on the look. Design booth experiences and giveaways, like our Educator Box, that pull educators in and leave a strong impression. Coordinate recognition moments that build goodwill with the educator community.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;New user and educator outreach&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drive first-time educator sign-ups and activations through on-site demos, hands-on experiences, and clear onboarding pathways. Partner with marketing on pre-event outreach and post-event nurture to convert conference contacts into active users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead capture and follow-through&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own badge scan setup, contact deduplication, and CRM upload. Build structured post-event reports tracking reach, engagement quality, and new user metrics. Route contacts to the right follow-up sequences based on educator type and interest level.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project tracking and budget management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Maintain conference timelines in Asana. Track budgets against actuals and reconcile expenses. Research new event opportunities based on audience fit and potential for educator reach, not just attendance numbers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What a Typical Show Looks Like&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;3 days on the floor, a 10x10 or 10x20 booth, 2 to 3 Epic staff and 2 Fellows, 1 sponsored session, 1 or 2 author signings, an Educator Box giveaway, and a lead target.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Planning starts about 12 weeks out and wraps 30 days after the show, with the busiest stretch in the final 6 weeks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Shows come a few weeks apart, so you will usually have two or three in flight at once.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who We Are Looking For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;3 to 5 years running event, trade show or conference operations end to end, in any industry. You have owned exhibitor kits, decorator orders, shipping and on-site logistics yourself, not just supported someone who did.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A track record of hitting deadlines across several events at once, with a system you can show us (Asana, Monday, Trello, a very good spreadsheet).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Comfortable on the phone and in email with decorators, venues, publishers, hotels and freight carriers, and clear enough in writing that a status update is four bullets, not four paragraphs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Careful with money: order forms, card authorizations, receipts and budget reconciliation are done right the first time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Remote and self-directed, with reliable overlap with Eastern and Pacific time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Able to travel to 2 to 4 shows a year for on-site support (about 10 to 15 percent).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;EdTech, K-12 or education conference experience (ISTE, FETC, TCEA, NCTE, state affiliates).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience sourcing booth displays, graphics or signage, or working with a creative team on event materials.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead retrieval and post-event lead workflows (badge scanners, deduplication, CRM or Iterable uploads).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Swag and print vendor management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Comfortable using AI tools like Claude or ChatGPT in your day-to-day work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;$43 to $50 per hour&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;About Epic School Plus&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Epic is the world&#39;s largest digital library for kids. Epic School Plus is the paid school and district version of Epic. It gives schools and districts administrator visibility through the Admin Portal, 24/7 and year-round access to 40,000+ books (including offline reading), more than 3,500 Spanish, Mandarin and French titles, and decodables for beginning readers aligned to 23 popular literacy curricula, including CKLA, UFLI and Benchmark Advance. When a district funds access, every family gets the same library at no cost to families.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Over one million teachers already use Epic School (free version) in their classrooms. Your job is to help the schools and districts behind them make Epic School Plus part of their reading plan.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a District Sales Specialist, you&#39;ll serve as one of the first points of contact for schools and districts interested in Epic School Plus. The role involves leading discovery calls and product walkthroughs with principals, curriculum and literacy directors, instructional coaches, and librarians, while following up on larger district opportunities to help move them through the district budget cycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position works closely with our operations team, which handles quotes and provisioning, as well as our sales lead for the Northeast and Midwest.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;part-time contract role, working 20 to 30 hours per week&lt;/strong&gt;, with approximately 25 to 30 hours a week from January through May, when districts plan budgets and approve purchases, and 20 to 25 hours a week from June through December.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run discovery calls and walkthroughs (about half your time):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;respond quickly to schools and districts that ask for a call, learn who champions, who builds the case and who signs, and show how Epic School Plus fits their reading goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Follow up on larger district opportunities (about a third of your time):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;re-engage open opportunities, find the decision-makers, keep stages and close dates accurate, and close out opportunities that aren&#39;t moving.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keep the talk track sharp:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;maintain our discovery script, walkthrough and objection guide, and share what you hear from educators so our marketing and product teams can act on it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keep the CRM clean:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;log every call, contact and next step in Salesforce so the team can see what&#39;s happening in each account.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience in B2B sales, preferably within EdTech or the K–12 education industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Confidence leading video calls with school and district leaders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Clear, warm writing for follow-up emails and notes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working knowledge of how districts buy: budget planning, board approvals and purchase orders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hands-on experience using Salesforce to manage sales activities and track opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Availability during Eastern or Central business hours, with flexibility to work more hours in spring.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Willingness to travel approximately 10% of the time for conferences and other events.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Previous experience as a teacher or librarian.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with Clever and ClassLink rostering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bilingual proficiency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;$30 to $40 per hour.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 3 []&quot;&gt;About Epic&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Epic is a digital reading platform for kids, giving children instant access to thousands of high-quality books, audiobooks, and learning videos. Teachers and librarians across the country use Epic School Plus to build reading habits in their classrooms. Our mission is to spark curiosity and a lifelong love of reading in every child.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Position Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Integration Specialist is responsible for the successful implementation, configuration, monitoring, troubleshooting, and ongoing maintenance of Epic School Plus integrations with third-party platforms, including Clever, ClassLink, and SchoolDay.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Integration Specialist works directly with school and district technology administrators and collaborates with Partner Success, Customer Experience, Product, Engineering, Sales, and external integration partners to resolve technical issues and improve the overall customer experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate combines technical troubleshooting skills with strong communication, organization, and customer service abilities. They can investigate complex data and access issues, explain technical concepts clearly to non-technical audiences, and take ownership of issues through resolution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Set up, configure, and launch Clever and ClassLink integrations (rostering and SSO) for new and renewing school and district customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Serve as the technical point of contact for district IT admins during onboarding, from data-sharing approval to first successful sync.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Troubleshoot sync and login issues: missing students, duplicate accounts, incorrect class or teacher associations, and SSO errors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Monitor integration health across accounts and proactively fix sync failures before they affect classrooms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Manage the Epic apps in the Clever and ClassLink partner portals, including app settings, data-sharing scopes, and district requests.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with Engineering to reproduce bugs, write clear tickets, and test fixes and new integration features.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coach Customer Success, Support, and Sales on how integrations work and how to set expectations with customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build and maintain help-center articles, internal runbooks, and setup guides for admins and teachers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Track integration metrics (time to launch, sync error rates, ticket volume) and recommend process improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support back-to-school peaks, when rostering volume is highest.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;2+ years in a technical support, implementation, or integration role, ideally in K–12 edtech.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hands-on experience administering or supporting Clever and/or ClassLink (rostering, SSO, or both).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Solid understanding of K–12 rostering data: students, teachers, sections, schools, and how a student information system (SIS) feeds them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working knowledge of SSO concepts (OAuth, SAML) and identity providers like Google Workspace and Microsoft Entra ID.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Comfort working with CSVs, spreadsheets, and API responses to diagnose data issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Clear, patient communication with both non-technical teachers and district IT staff.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong organization: you can run many district setups in parallel and keep each one moving.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with student data privacy requirements (FERPA, COPPA, state privacy agreements).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Clever or ClassLink certification, or prior work at either company or a district using them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with other rostering standards and tools: OneRoster, Google Classroom, Microsoft Teams for Education, or SIS platforms like PowerSchool and Infinite Campus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Basic SQL or scripting (Python, JavaScript) for data checks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with Zendesk, Salesforce, Jira, or similar tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Background as a teacher, school technology coordinator, or district IT admin.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Compensation:&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;$35–$40&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;per&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;hour,&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;up&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;to&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;30&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;hours&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;per&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;week.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 3 []&quot;&gt;About Epic&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Epic Kids is the leading digital reading platform built for kids 12 and under, trusted by millions of children, educators, and families around the world. Our mission is to inspire a lifelong love of reading by providing unlimited access to thousands of high-quality books, videos, and educational content through a safe and engaging experience. We combine technology, storytelling, and learning innovation to help every child become a confident reader.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Epic, you&#39;ll join a collaborative and fast-paced global team passionate about building meaningful products that make a real impact on children&#39;s education and literacy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Engagement&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We need a hands-on Iterable expert to get our educator email journeys live, running correctly, and measured, and to shape an email engagement strategy across our user segments. Our new educator onboarding journey creative was finished in February and is still not fully live because of Iterable and product setup. More educator journeys are queued behind it, and we have had to pause journeys that sent when they should not have. Recent campaign sends have also shown gaps in our wider email process, such as sends reaching the wrong countries or listing the wrong dates, so we also need email marketing operations help to fix how campaigns get built, checked and approved.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a 12-week contract. You&#39;ll work alongside our Email team and partner with Product and Engineering on event data. The goal is to clear the backlog, prevent new mistakes, and leave us with a strategy and playbook we can run ourselves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Own&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;true&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Educator Journey Launch:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Finish setup, QA and launch of the new educator onboarding journey, and retire the old one with no gap in coverage. Then build and launch the other educator journeys in progress, in priority order. Monitor each launch and report results against our journey goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Iterable Audit &amp;amp; QA:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Audit active journeys and campaigns, and flag anything sending to the wrong audience or overlapping another program. Put a pre-launch QA checklist and sign-off step in place so unintended sends stop.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Email Marketing Operations Review:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Review how our email campaigns move from request to send today across Marketing, Creative, Product and the Email team. Find where errors slip through and recommend improvements, such as clear owners and checks for audience, country, dates and offers before anything sends. Help put the agreed changes in place. Start from the issues the team has already flagged in the weekly email marketing meeting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conversion Tracking:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Review our educator and family conversion definitions and tracking in Iterable, and implement or fix them where needed, with tracking live by December 1. Confirm the product events our journeys rely on to reach Iterable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SMS Integration:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Help complete the Iterable SMS setup and define the first educator SMS use case, opt-in and compliance requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engagement Strategy Across Segments:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Map current email by segment: free and paid educators, ES+ schools and districts, families, and prospects. Recommend programs, cadence and priority rules so programs don&#39;t collide, plus a roadmap for the next two quarters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documentation &amp;amp; Handoff:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Leave a playbook covering journey logic, naming, QA and troubleshooting, and walk the Email team through it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Timeline &amp;amp; Deliverables&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Weeks 1–2:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Iterable walkthrough, audit of live journeys, QA checklist, prioritized launch list, review of the current email campaign process&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Weeks 3–8:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;onboarding journey live and monitored, next journeys launched, conversion tracking live by Dec 1, process improvements recommended and rolling out&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Weeks 9–12:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;segment strategy and roadmap, playbook, final walkthrough&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Weekly:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;30-minute check-in and a short written status update&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Not in scope:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;email creative and copy, product or engineering builds, changing email platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;3+ years hands-on in Iterable: journeys, segmentation, triggers, data feeds and QA&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lifecycle email experience across several user segments&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience setting up conversion or event tracking and reporting on email impact&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Email marketing operations experience: campaign intake, workflows, QA and approvals across teams&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Clear, practical recommendations, delivered collaboratively with an in-house team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Comfortable working remotely and independently&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;EdTech, K-12 or freemium product experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Iterable SMS setup&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salesforce and Iterable integrations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deliverability and domain reputation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;How We&#39;ll Measure Success&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Educator onboarding journey live, old journey retired, no coverage gap&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No unintended sends from journeys launched or reviewed&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Process improvements agreed and in use, with audience, country and dates checked before every send&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Conversion tracking live in Iterable by December 1&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every in-progress educator journey launched or on a dated plan&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Segment strategy and playbook delivered and reviewed by the Email team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 3 []&quot;&gt;About Epic&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Epic is a digital reading platform for kids 12 and under, with a library of high-quality children’s books, audiobooks, and read-to-me titles. Epic is free for educators, and teachers and librarians across the U.S. use it every day to get kids reading more, with more joy. Many of our biggest champions are school librarians and ELA teachers who brought Epic into their buildings on their own.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Strategic Partnerships Specialist, you’ll be Epic’s local, in-person presence in your community, based in the&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;San Francisco Bay Area&lt;/strong&gt;. Your mission: help more educators discover Epic, bring it into their classrooms and libraries, and make reading with Epic part of their everyday routine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work with schools and districts in your area, building relationships with teachers, librarians, and school communities. You’ll help educators who already love Epic share it with their colleagues, support teachers as they get started, and introduce Epic to schools that haven’t discovered it yet. This is a grassroots, educator-to-educator role. Epic is free for educators, so this isn’t about selling. It’s about being a trusted local voice who shows teachers how Epic fits into their day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Along the way, you’ll share what you learn in the field and help shape the school partnership playbook that guides this work as it expands to new markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;What you’ll do&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Bay Area literacy and education technology initiatives&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Epic’s school partnership work in the Bay Area: build work plans, set milestones, and coordinate with Epic’s partnerships, product and marketing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Launch and lead an Epic Educator Advisory Group of principals, assistant principals, instructional coaches, librarians and teachers. Turn its input into clear recommendations for Epic’s leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help school and district leaders connect Epic to their literacy goals, such as foundational reading, independent reading time, English learner support and summer reading&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Epic as a practitioner voice at conferences, county office of education events, district convenings and literacy partner events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design and facilitate educator training&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and lead in-person and virtual professional learning on reading engagement, classroom technology use and family literacy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate sessions at staff meetings, PD days, literacy and family nights, and library events, spending 2–3 days a week at schools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Give follow-up coaching after trainings so teachers move from first use to regular classroom routines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead family sessions in English and your second language, with a focus on schools that serve multilingual learners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build strategic school and district partnerships&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own relationships with leaders across a portfolio of 10–15 priority Bay Area districts and their elementary and K–8 schools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Move schools from individual teacher use to school-wide adoption by working with principals, librarians and teacher champions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help districts add Epic to approved app lists, and connect them with Epic’s team on data privacy agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build partnerships with public libraries, literacy nonprofits and community organizations that support young readers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Create resources and support instruction&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain training materials, school toolkits, family resources and Epic’s school partnership playbook&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adapt resources for multilingual families and different school contexts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find and lift up standout educators for recognition and case studies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run program operations and share what you learn&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track school visits, training attendance, adoption and reading activity, and use that data to decide where to focus next&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather feedback from trainings and evaluate what’s working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share regular, specific insight on school priorities, literacy needs and product gaps with Epic’s team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;What you bring&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in K–8 education, including at least 2 years as an assistant principal, principal, dean, district strategist, instructional coach lead or in a similar leadership role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years leading major projects or school-wide initiatives, such as a literacy program, technology rollout or PD series&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bilingual in English and at least one language widely spoken in Bay Area schools, such as Spanish, Cantonese, Mandarin, Vietnamese, Tagalog or Arabic. You can present to and coach families and educators in that language.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and facilitating adult learning, both in person and virtually&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active relationships with Bay Area school and district leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong public speaking skills and comfort facilitating groups of senior educators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organized and self-directed, able to manage competing priorities; comfortable with Google Workspace, spreadsheets and basic data tracking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reliable transportation and willingness to travel regularly to schools across the Bay Area&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;How we’ll measure success&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New teacher and librarian sign-ups in your portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Activated teachers: classes created, students added, and kids reading&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth in active teachers and daily student reading across your schools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Schools moving up tiers, from a single user toward school-wide adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;School visits, educator meetings, and presentations delivered&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quality of field insights contributed to the playbook&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we provide&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Onboarding and training on Epic, plus ongoing support from the Educator Engagement team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Usage data and a prioritized school list for your portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Presentation decks, one-pagers, printed materials, and Epic swag&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coverage of approved travel, meals, and materials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation and terms&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;$50 per hour and quarterly bonus of up to $5K based on target achievement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Time commitment:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;25 - 30 hours per week, with 2 to 3 days in schools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Start date:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;November 2, 2026 (flexible)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commute:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Mileage reimbursed based on actuals as per IRS standards ($72.5 cents per mile)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

