&lt;h2 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;About Epic&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Epic Kids is the leading digital reading platform built for kids 12 and under, trusted by millions of children, educators, and families around the world. Our mission is to inspire a lifelong love of reading by providing unlimited access to thousands of high-quality books, videos, and educational content through a safe and engaging experience. We combine technology, storytelling, and learning innovation to help every child become a confident reader.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Epic, you&#39;ll join a collaborative and fast-paced global team passionate about building meaningful products that make a real impact on children&#39;s education and literacy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll own Epic&#39;s native Android app, the main way kids open a book on Android phones, tablets and Chromebooks. It&#39;s a large, mature Kotlin codebase with some Java and xml UI layouts. You&#39;ll work independently and partner closely with our Android, iOS, backend and web engineers and with the US engineering team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own and evolve the Android app across phones, tablets and Chromebooks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the reading experience: our in-house page renderer and page-flip animation, zoom and gestures, and Read-to-Me audio synced to word highlighting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own offline reading (encrypted downloads, background work, local storage), Google Play Billing subscriptions, and the Play Store release pipeline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drive performance, stability and quality: startup time, memory, ANRs and crashes, and test coverage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Modernize carefully: move legacy Java and RxJava code forward without breaking a live app. also move to compose UIs whenever possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Over time, pick up some iOS/Swift work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;4 - 6 years of building and shipping native Android apps.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong Kotlin, and comfortable working in mixed Kotlin and Java code.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deep experience with the Android View system, Fragments and custom Views: custom drawing, animation and touch handling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reactive and async programming: RxJava 2 in production, plus Kotlin coroutines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dependency injection, MVP or MVVM architecture and Networking with Retrofit and OkHttp.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Local persistence with Room/SQLite, including schema migrations, and background work with WorkManager.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Google Play Billing and the release pipeline: Gradle build variants, app signing, CI (Jenkins or similar), Play Console tracks and staged rollouts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Testing with JUnit, Mockito or MockK, Robolectric and Espresso.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Media: ExoPlayer/Media3, MediaPlayer, and syncing audio to text.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Handling encrypted media and content stored offline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Jetpack Compose, and the judgment to know when it fits alongside an existing View-based codebase.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Performance tooling: Perfetto, Android Studio profilers, LeakCanary, New Relic or Crashlytics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with kids&#39; or education apps and children&#39;s privacy rules (COPPA).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Interest in cross-platform mobile and some familiarity with iOS/Swift.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;40–50 LPA, with some flexibility for exceptional candidates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2 class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot; data-section-id=&quot;16kvosu&quot; data-start=&quot;171&quot; data-end=&quot;182&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;184&quot; data-end=&quot;636&quot;&gt;Epic Kids is the leading digital reading platform built for kids 12 and under, trusted by millions of children, educators, and families around the world. Our mission is to inspire a lifelong love of reading by providing unlimited access to thousands of high-quality books, videos, and educational content through a safe and engaging experience. We combine technology, storytelling, and learning innovation to help every child become a confident reader.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;638&quot; data-end=&quot;809&quot;&gt;At Epic, you&#39;ll join a collaborative and fast-paced global team passionate about building meaningful products that make a real impact on children&#39;s education and literacy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-section-id=&quot;1wct3r9&quot; data-start=&quot;811&quot; data-end=&quot;828&quot;&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;830&quot; data-end=&quot;1115&quot;&gt;The Senior iOS Engineer owns Epic&#39;s native iOS app -- the primary way our readers open a book on iPhone and iPad. You work independently on a large, established Swift and Objective-C codebase, own the reading experience end-to-end, and partner with our Android, backend, and web teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1117&quot; data-end=&quot;1222&quot;&gt;This is a role based in India, working closely with Epic&#39;s US engineering team and the wider global team.&lt;/p&gt;
